#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087391 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8edbecf-59d3-5f32-a0ac-d6e8f2128dc0" :knowledge-point/title "Transforming a Homogeneous Differential Equation into a Separable Equation Using a Substitution"}] :question/id #uuid "34c357f1-505b-530f-8bb4-376eada248a9" :question/math-academy-id "e-2301" :question/problem "Use the transformation $y = vx$ (where $v=v(x)$) to rewrite the given first-order homogeneous ODE\n$\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} = \\cos \\left(\\frac {y} {x} \\right)$\nas a separable ODE in $v$ and $x$." :question/worked-solution "With $y = vx$ (where $v = v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx} = x\\frac{dv}{dx} + v\n$$\n\nPlugging that into the differential equation and separating variables, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\cos (\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\\nx\\frac{dv}{dx} + v &= \\cos (v) \\\\\nx\\frac{dv}{dx} &= \\cos (v) - v \\\\\n((1)/(\\cos (v) - v))\\frac{dv}{dx} &= \\frac{1}{x}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087392 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49eaf082-07de-5468-a2d7-4cdfce27a553" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Differential Equation"}] :question/id #uuid "89b7276c-ef41-5123-ad31-b54753656111" :question/math-academy-id "e-2302" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n$\\frac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\frac{x^2+y^2}{2xy}$." :question/worked-solution "We note that this equation is a homogeneous first-order differential equation because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(tx, ty) &= ((tx)^{2} + (ty)^{2})/(2(tx)(ty)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{t^{2}x^{2} + t^{2}y^{2}}{2t^{2}y} \\\\\n&= \\frac{x^{2} + y^{2}}{2xy} \\\\\n&= f(x, y)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe given equation is not separable, but we can transform it into a separable equation by carrying out the substitution\n\n$$\ny=vx, \\quad \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = v + x \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}v}{\\textrm{d}x} \\,\n$$\n\nCarrying out the substitution and separating variables, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{x^{2} + y^{2}}{2xy} \\\\\nv + x\\frac{dv}{dx} &= (x^{2} + (vx)^{2})/(2x(vx)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{x^{2} + v^{2}x^{2}}{2x^{2}v} \\\\\n&= (x^{2}(1 + v^{2}))/(2x^{2}v) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1 + v^{2}}{2v} \\\\\nx\\frac{dv}{dx} &= \\frac{1 + v^{2}}{2v} - v \\\\\n&= \\frac{1 + v^{2}}{2v} - \\frac{2v^{2}}{2v} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1 - v^{2}}{2v} \\\\\n\\frac{2v}{1 - v^{2}}\\frac{dv}{dx} &= \\frac{1}{x}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\frac{2v}{1 - v^{2}}\\frac{dv}{dx}dx &= ∫\\frac{1}{x}dx \\\\\n∫\\frac{2v}{1 - v^{2}}dv &= \\ln\\begin{vmatrix}x & + C_{1} \\\\ -\\ln & 1 - v^{2}\\end{vmatrix}|= \\ln \\mid C_{2}x \\mid \\\\\n\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{1}{1 - v^{2}} & &= \\ln & C_{2}x\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n\\frac{1}{1 - v^{2}} &= C_{2}x \\\\\n1 - v^{2} &= \\frac{1}{C_{2}x} \\\\\n1 - v^{2} &= \\frac{C_{3}}{x}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nC_1=\\ln{C_2}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{C_2}=C_3\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting\n\n$$\nv=\\dfrac{y}{x}\n$$\n\nand simplifying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1 - v^{2} &= \\frac{C_{3}}{x} \\\\\n1 - (\\frac{y}{x})^{2} &= \\frac{C_{3}}{x} \\\\\n1 - \\frac{y^{2}}{x^{2}} &= \\frac{C_{3}}{x} \\\\\n\\frac{y^{2}}{x^{2}} &= 1 - \\frac{C_{3}}{x} \\\\\n\\frac{y^{2}}{x^{2}} &= 1 + \\frac{C_{4}}{x} \\\\\ny^{2} &= x^{2}(1 + \\frac{C_{4}}{x}) \\\\\ny^{2} &= x^{2} + C_{4}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C_4 = -C_3$. Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{2} &= x^{2} + C_{4}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087393 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e8c2a855-07a3-5855-9f6c-1a914953ac53" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Homogeneous Differential Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "f34de8cd-b650-5926-9f06-8127d4fb3a55" :question/math-academy-id "e-2393" :question/problem "Which of the following differential equations are homogeneous?\n\n1. $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{y}{x}$\n2. $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{y}{x^2}$\n3. $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{y}{2x}\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{x^2}{y^2}\\right)}$" :question/worked-solution "A first-order ordinary differential equation that is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} = f(x, y)\n$$\n\nis said to be homogeneous if $f(x,y)$ is a homogeneous function of degree zero, meaning that it satisfies\n\n$$\nf(tx, ty) = f(x, y)\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at the right-hand side function in each differential equation.\n\n- The function $f(x,y) = \\dfrac{y}{x}$ is a homogeneous function of degree zero:\n$f(tx, ty)|= ((ty))/((tx)); = \\frac{t \\cdot y}{t \\cdot x}; = \\frac{y}{x}; = f(x, y)✓$\nTherefore, equation I is a homogenous differential equation.\n- The function $f(x,y) = \\dfrac{y}{x^2}$ is *not* a homogeneous function of degree $0$. Rather, it is a homogeneous function of degree $-1$:\n$f(tx, ty)|= ((ty))/((tx)^{2}); = \\frac{t \\cdot y}{t^{2} \\cdot x^{2}}; = \\frac{1}{t} \\cdot \\frac{y}{x^{2}}; = \\frac{1}{t} \\cdot f(x, y); = t^{-1}f(x, y)\\cdot$\nTherefore, equation II is *not* a homogenous differential equation.\n- The function $f(x,y) = \\dfrac{y}{2x}\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{x^2}{y^2}\\right)}$ is a homogeneous function of degree zero:\n$f(tx, ty)|= (ty)/(2(tx))\\sin (((tx)^{2})/((ty)^{2})); = \\frac{t \\cdot y}{t \\cdot 2x}\\sin (\\frac{t^{2}x^{2}}{t^{2}y^{2}}); = \\frac{y}{2x}\\sin (\\frac{x^{2}}{y^{2}}); = f(x, y)✓$\nTherefore, equation III is a homogenous differential equation.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087947 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8edbecf-59d3-5f32-a0ac-d6e8f2128dc0" :knowledge-point/title "Transforming a Homogeneous Differential Equation into a Separable Equation Using a Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87478308-c312-590d-830c-feaf4cb1cdce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{v + 1}{2v^{3} - v^{2}})\\frac{dv}{dx} = x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084694} {:answer/id #uuid "9487561f-2063-58ea-bc91-b5107e10b5e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{2v^{2} - v}{v + 1})\\frac{dv}{dx} = x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084695} {:answer/id #uuid "b1ad20f9-2688-55d2-9b72-dffd56a10e11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{v^{2} + v}{3v^{2} - v})\\frac{dv}{dx} = \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084696} {:answer/id #uuid "e267c795-b678-5b29-ae42-d19aa0f83aad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{v + 1}{2v^{2} - v})\\frac{dv}{dx} = \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084697} {:answer/id #uuid "7de5aeb5-dce7-537d-a056-e779ff6f08b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{v + 1}{v^{2} + 1})\\frac{dv}{dx} = \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084698}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e267c795-b678-5b29-ae42-d19aa0f83aad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{v + 1}{2v^{2} - v})\\frac{dv}{dx} = \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084697} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd82c334-5f7b-5744-9a4b-62ade8bea1d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084693}] :question/id #uuid "695b49d1-9327-503a-b244-1f7f385f59ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-14315" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{3y^{3}}{xy^{2} + yx^{2}}$.\n\nIf the transformation $y = v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088381 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e8c2a855-07a3-5855-9f6c-1a914953ac53" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Homogeneous Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b387a19d-7cf7-5c7c-b4a0-3c531f2dc207" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{x^{2}y}{x^{2} + y^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087217} {:answer/id #uuid "c5fc4204-9ff1-5434-b8c8-b243a9b5a4ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{2xy}{x^{2} + y^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087218} {:answer/id #uuid "e8891a45-78f7-5a8b-a02d-8cc9d4f8af08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{x^{2}y^{2}}{x^{2} + y^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087219} {:answer/id #uuid "37572047-280a-508a-ac11-6a5fe1712a8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{xy^{2}}{x^{2} + y^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087220} {:answer/id #uuid "7253b068-0bec-5847-aaa9-da6e7449baf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{xy}{x + y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5fc4204-9ff1-5434-b8c8-b243a9b5a4ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{2xy}{x^{2} + y^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087218} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc06f993-8bb8-5bba-9060-505b57e636e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087216}] :question/id #uuid "32964a8b-4376-5c16-9f30-00e530a869bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-8739" :question/problem "Which of the following is a first-order homogeneous ordinary differential equation?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088382 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e8c2a855-07a3-5855-9f6c-1a914953ac53" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Homogeneous Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87971271-4d9c-5148-b3f3-1acf321db5ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\ln y - \\ln x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087223} {:answer/id #uuid "936de1db-5ead-5221-8763-8a6f4805dd21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx} = 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087224} {:answer/id #uuid "b4487aa0-cf0d-5d85-a6d9-c074d3f1ab09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087225} {:answer/id #uuid "bfceb5b2-39ab-518b-a918-f750fa8a0fc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\arctan (\\frac{x}{y})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087226} {:answer/id #uuid "24ac0309-cf10-5637-9bcf-a86d99411716" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx} = x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24ac0309-cf10-5637-9bcf-a86d99411716" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx} = x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087227} :answer-field/id #uuid "39550c0d-6eec-516e-a844-c07d2d66ac51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087222}] :question/id #uuid "8c38fa75-d73d-55f8-bbc1-1dea4b79194b" :question/math-academy-id "q-8741" :question/problem "Which of the following is NOT a first-order homogeneous ordinary differential equation?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088383 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8edbecf-59d3-5f32-a0ac-d6e8f2128dc0" :knowledge-point/title "Transforming a Homogeneous Differential Equation into a Separable Equation Using a Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6e97ce9-c081-5657-b3e5-e7caf27c56f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos (\\frac{1}{v})\\frac{dv}{dx} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087229} {:answer/id #uuid "1720e445-6185-51bb-b6b2-c55c33e085a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1)/(\\cos (\\frac{1}{v}))\\frac{dv}{dx} = x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087230} {:answer/id #uuid "1f30805d-8881-530c-95e1-379ad6645d35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1)/(2v + \\sec (\\frac{1}{v}))\\frac{dv}{dx} = \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087231} {:answer/id #uuid "344e9adb-82ae-5a75-98af-5a3132c81eef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1)/(v + \\sec (\\frac{1}{v}))\\frac{dv}{dx} = \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087232} {:answer/id #uuid "46f3e85c-d308-5ac8-b3f6-ea8506b85056" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos (\\frac{1}{v})\\frac{dv}{dx} = \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46f3e85c-d308-5ac8-b3f6-ea8506b85056" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos (\\frac{1}{v})\\frac{dv}{dx} = \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087233} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef9ba045-f0a9-505f-bdbd-1bbeecdbcdd8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087228}] :question/id #uuid "6aa0e045-65b8-5bd8-8a66-10e8e133beb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-8745" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\sec (\\frac{x}{y}) + \\frac{y}{x}$.\n\nIf the transformation $y = v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088388 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49eaf082-07de-5468-a2d7-4cdfce27a553" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0745565-b7ab-5796-a081-2e46424ec253" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{2} =-x^{3} + Cx^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087259} {:answer/id #uuid "d7b1d5a4-fd99-5c6f-b68a-4d082f11c047" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{2} =-x^{2}\\ln x^{2} + Cx^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087260} {:answer/id #uuid "d9cd2778-2a05-50a8-ba1f-5b723f108297" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{2} = x\\ln (Cx^{3} + x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087261} {:answer/id #uuid "5a5d1b52-ebe2-507d-9303-9e229260de7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{2} = x\\ln x + Cx^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087262} {:answer/id #uuid "7ec3a65d-b7cc-54bc-bedf-f31eb32640f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{3} = x^{2}\\ln (x^{2} + Cx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7b1d5a4-fd99-5c6f-b68a-4d082f11c047" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{2} =-x^{2}\\ln x^{2} + Cx^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087260} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ef6d8a2-5d7c-511b-8c0a-8a924bf134a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087258}] :question/id #uuid "19530196-afb6-5c10-98a9-988afc75a28c" :question/math-academy-id "q-8844" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the following differential equation.\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{y^{2} - x^{2}}{xy}$"}]}
